,"validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how canonical preview obtains a coherent read-only view while a concurrent lock-holding sync/live pass mutates the same store (e.g. atomic snapshot of the source ref taken once), and cover the read-during-write case in the test plan or explicitly justify why torn reads cannot occur.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Context: 'The canonical route will load a coherent read-only snapshot and produce its manifest without acquiring, purging, stealing, or writing the pass lock.'","Test plan: 'No contention harness is added because preview removes a lock rather than composing writes, while sync continues through the existing single pass lock.'","ABSENCE: no stated mechanism (e.g., atomic git-ref read / immutable snapshot handle) by which the lock-free preview reader observes a coherent view while a lock-holding writer mutates concurrently."],"finding":"Canonical preview becomes a lock-free reader ('load a coherent read-only snapshot ... without acquiring ... the pass lock'), but the plan does not specify how snapshot coherence is guaranteed when a concurrent capped/uncapped sync or legacy live pass holds the pass lock and is mutating the same store. The test plan explicitly declines a contention harness ('preview removes a lock rather than composing writes'), which addresses write-write contention but not the read-during-write torn-snapshot case.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f795338320c4e2c4c","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context ('load a coherent read-only snapshot') and Test plan ('No contention harness is added because preview removes a lock rather than composing writes')","norm_id":"n56e353162881c247","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A sync/live pass is mid-write applying mutations while a canonical preview runs lock-free and reads a partially-updated ref/state, producing a manifest reflecting a torn snapshot."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Specify that preview resolves and reads from a single immutable snapshot (e.g. a captured commit/ref SHA) taken atomically at pass entry, and add a test asserting the manifest reflects that pinned snapshot even if the underlying refs advance during the read.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the canonical envelope renderer extends the existing render_dry_run_or_strict (which already enumerates inbound field detail via _enumerate_inbound) or is a genuinely new shape, and justify a separate renderer rather than reusing/parameterizing the existing one.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["manifest_renderer.py:106-127 render_dry_run_or_strict already enumerates inbound via _enumerate_inbound with 'fields': _payload_of(m)","reconcile_helpers.py:437-467 _build_plan_entries already builds per-mut